<title>HONG KONG: Wah Lee debuts at HK$1.30 per share.</title>
<headline>Wah Lee debuts at HK$1.30 per share.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of air conditioning systems, audio visual and photographic products distributor Wah Lee Resources Holdings Ltd made their trading debut at HK$1.30 per share on Friday, compared with the issue price of HK$1.00.  </p>
<p>Wah Lee offered 70 million shares at HK$1.00 each in an initial public offering (IPO) in Hong Kong. One warrant was attached for every five shares subscribed.</p>
<p>Its IPO was 32.6 times subscribed.</p>
<p>The company had said net proceeds would be used to promote products, set up product display showrooms across China, to buy a warehouse in Hong Kong and for working capital.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
